IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-section-definitions`

-- Tests for act-section-definitions.l4.
-- The form of each definition is read from its first line: "means", "includes", "means ... and includes", "—see" or none of those.

§ `Tests: definitions inside sections`

-- s 15 (3), definition of law: law—see section 107 (Definitions—ch 11).
#ASSERT `s 15 (3), definition of law`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `a signpost definition`
#ASSERT `s 15 (3), definition of law`'s `term` EQUALS "law"
#ASSERT `s 15 (3), definition of law`'s `further lines as printed` EQUALS EMPTY
-- s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment: former Commonwealth enactment means a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or Imperi
#ASSERT `s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
#ASSERT `s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment`'s `term` EQUALS "former Commonwealth enactment"
#ASSERT elem "(a) an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34; or" (`s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment`'s `further lines as printed`)
-- s 72, definition of law: law means an Act or statutory instrument.
